Why Is Demand Increasing?
Rapid mobile adoption: Mobile-first platforms are becoming the primary channel for online betting and gambling activity.
Increasing internet penetration: Wider access to smartphones and mobile broadband is expanding the global user base.
Regulatory liberalization: New licensing frameworks in emerging markets are opening additional opportunities for operators.
AI-powered platforms: AI and machine learning are improving odds modeling, personalization and fraud detection.
Growth of eSports betting: Competitive gaming is creating a new betting ecosystem with strong engagement among younger audiences.
Digital payment adoption: Mobile wallets and cryptocurrency-based payment systems are simplifying transactions.
Digital Betting Technology Watch
The Online Gambling and Betting Market is increasingly shaped by mobile-first experiences, AI analytics and immersive digital technologies. The report indicates that mobile-first platforms generated approximately 70% of total betting turnover in 2025.
AI-driven odds modeling is also becoming an important competitive tool. Operators using AI-powered risk assessment can improve betting margins by approximately 4%, while personalization engines help improve user engagement.
eSports betting is another major opportunity, contributing close to 15% of total revenue growth and recording session lengths approximately 20% longer than traditional sports betting.
