Regional Outlook
North America was the largest market in 2025, supported by expanding legal sports betting and iGaming markets.
Europe remains a major established market with strong operator presence and mature online gambling infrastructure.
Emerging markets in Latin America and Africa are attracting investment following regulatory liberalization.
Asia-Pacific offers significant long-term opportunities as internet and smartphone penetration increases.
Jurisdictions with clear licensing and consumer-protection frameworks are becoming increasingly attractive to operators.
Why This Market Matters
Online gambling and betting platforms are becoming increasingly data-driven and mobile-centric. Operators can use AI to optimize odds, identify suspicious activity, personalize offers and improve customer engagement.
However, responsible gambling and regulatory compliance remain critical. Operators are increasingly required to provide self-exclusion tools, spending limits and real-time loss information.
The market also faces legal uncertainty because regulations vary significantly across countries and, in some cases, between individual states or jurisdictions.
